course: dictionary
lesson: 4782
title: Huge and very big
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «Huge» means very, very big. You can use it for size, like a huge dog, for amount, like a huge pile of homework, or for importance, like a huge mistake. When you read it, picture something much bigger than normal.
explain: Look at the words around «huge» to check its meaning. «The Great Sphinx is a huge statue with a lion's body and a pharaoh's head.» A statue with a lion's body is a big thing, so huge means very big in size here.
explain: «Huge» is not an exact number. It tells you that something is much bigger than usual, but not how big. If you need an exact amount, use numbers. «Québec» is not just a huge place: the French traded furs across huge distances, so the distances were very long.
fact: Huge means very, very big in size, amount or importance.
fact: «Huge» is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like a huge dog.
fact: «Huge» does not give an exact number. Use numbers when you need to say exactly how big something is.
fact: «An African elephant's two huge ears» means its ears are very big, and they help to cool its blood.
fact: «Vent water can be hotter than three hundred degrees, but it does not boil because of the huge pressure of the deep sea.» Here huge means very strong, great in amount.
exercise: «The Great Sphinx is a huge statue with a lion's body.» What does huge mean here? | *Very big | Very small | Very old and broken | Very quiet
exercise: Jayden says «a huge mistake» means a tiny mistake. Who is right? | *Jayden is wrong, because huge means very big in importance | Jayden is right, because mistakes are always small | Nobody, because a mistake cannot be big | Jayden is right, because huge means tiny
exercise: «The beaver fur was so valuable that the beaver became a symbol of Canada.» Find and copy one word that means very big in size or amount. | valuable | beaver | *huge | symbol
test: «The Sun is huge compared with Earth.» Which word tells you the Sun is much bigger than usual? | Earth | *huge | the | compared
test: Which sentence uses huge to show great importance? | The cat sat by the window. | The teacher gave a short, quiet reply. | *The news was a huge surprise to everyone in the class. | My shoes are blue and white.
exam: «Huge» means very big, but it does not tell you an exact size. If you need an exact amount, which should you use? | The word huge again | A different adjective, like slow | A feeling | *Numbers
